# Making and moving
> AmigaDOS has MakeDir, Copy, Rename and Delete. vsh has `mkdir`, `cp`, `mv` and `rm`.
> Careful: `rm` deletes at once, and `rm -r` deletes a drawer with everything in it. Read the
> name twice before you press Return. Here you are in a practice drawer, so nothing of yours is at risk,
> but the same line would delete real files anywhere else.
? Make a drawer called projects (AmigaDOS: MakeDir).
= [ -d projects ]
~ Type mkdir projects.
! mkdir projects
? Make an empty file called orig.txt.
= [ -f orig.txt ]
~ touch makes an empty file: touch orig.txt.
! touch orig.txt
? Copy orig.txt to copy.txt (AmigaDOS: Copy).
= [ -f orig.txt ] && [ -f copy.txt ]
~ cp FROM TO: cp orig.txt copy.txt.
! cp orig.txt copy.txt
? Rename copy.txt to new.txt (AmigaDOS: Rename). mv moves and renames.
= [ -f new.txt ] && [ ! -e copy.txt ]
~ mv copy.txt new.txt.
! mv copy.txt new.txt
? Delete new.txt (AmigaDOS: Delete).
= [ ! -e new.txt ]
~ rm new.txt.
! rm new.txt
? Delete the drawer projects (AmigaDOS: Delete ALL).
= [ ! -d projects ]
~ A drawer needs -r: rm -r projects.
! rm -r projects
